# Lab Instrument Control — Project Rules

## Context
This is a Python codebase for laboratory instrument control, translated from MATLAB.
The MATLAB source lives in the `matlab/` root (read-only reference).
The Python target lives in the `pyctrl/` root.

## Python Version
- Target: Python 3.11
- Use 3.11-compatible syntax only; avoid 3.12+ features for now
- When 3.12 features would be meaningfully better, leave a comment: `# TODO: simplify with 3.12`

## Project Architecture reference
This section describes the overall architecture of the pyctrl codebase.
It is provided as context, not as a set of instructions. When writing
or translating code, follow the conventions in other sections, use this to understand where things live and why, and to provide suggestion and reminder if the project goes astray.

pyctrl/
├── configs/
│   ├── instr_config.toml           ← instrument names, classes, connection parameters
│   └── path_config.toml            ← local save paths (gitignored, commit .template version)
├── hwdrivers/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── instrumentsession.py        ← Session class: instrument lifecycle manager
│   └── <instname>/
│       ├── __init__.py
│       ├── <instname>.py           ← instrument driver class
│       ├── test_<instname>.py      ← connection/sanity test script
│       └── livetest_<instname>.ipynb  ← interactive notebook for hardware testing
├── experiments/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   └── <expname>.py                ← one file per experiment type
└── toolbox/
    ├── hardware/
    │   ├── __init__.py
    │   └── <routinename>.py        ← free functions requiring 2+ instruments
    └── software/
        ├── __init__.py
        ├── <routinename>.py        ← free functions requiring no instrument, purely software
        └── expdata.py              ← dataclasses for experiment output structures

- `hwdrivers/`  — one folder per instrument/instrument type, containing at least:
    - one main file describing the class-based driver for this instrument type
    - one test .py file testing connectivity and basic instrument functions. named test_classname
- `toolbox/hardware`   — reusable free functions acting on instrument hardware objects
- `toolbox/software`   — reusable free functions acting on data exclusively, no hardware interaction
- `experiments/` — lightweight experiment classes with a `run()` method
- keep the config file for instrument (default configdefault.toml) simple and clean, only one entry per intrument, don't worry about missnaming and case sensitivity, that's be fixed in debugging.


