## Style

- Follow PEP8; line length max 100 characters, wildcard up to 120 if it improves lisibility
- only import packages at the top of the file, never mid-way!
- Use type hints on all function signatures; omit on obvious local variables
- always use `logging`, never `print`
- No bare `except:` clauses — always catch a specific exception
- catching errors: use logging and logger.error or logger.critical, pass the specific exception / log the trace, and then simply raise
- Keep files under ~500 lines; split if larger
- keep the docstrings on all classes and public functions consise, focus on useful information on what the code does
- when importing packages that might be non-general/particular to an instrument etc (e.g. import serial), do NOT wrap the import in try-catch statements, trust that the package is available in the environment like any other package.
- all python files start by a comment signing the author and containing the date of creation (author: yannik fontana, creation date: dd.mm.yyyy)
- for every package/module `__init__.py`, the first instruction after imports must be: `__author__ = "yannik fontana"`